+# FleetPi
+
+A private workspace in the pinned Pi fork: real coding-agent sessions on Fleet, with hardware-aware request admission, durable progress and a terminal festival demo. Upstream Pi core is unchanged.
+
+The supported demo is Muse Glimmer 30B MLX affine four-bit on a 48 GB Apple silicon Mac. Common limits are 96,000 context tokens and 4,096 output tokens per response. The same real Pi file tools, browser tests and task facts are used by Fleet8, default-performance vLLM8 and vLLM1. Required Glimmer compatibility corrections are isolated from the installed backend.
+
+From the FleetLLM repository root:
+
+```sh
+python3 integrations/fleetpi/bootstrap.py
+make -j6
+./fleetpi
+./fleetpi demo festival
+```
+
+runFestival() exposes the same runner programmatically without starting a server. The CLI owns and stops one engine process group. beforeRun supports an awaited initial screenshot before any inference. Ctrl-C saves progress; resume uses atomic state, real Pi SessionManager transcripts and a hash-validated ledger. Interrupted comparisons resume one case with its explicit mode/output directory.
+
+Overall workflow success requires every staged round to pass. finalPassed separately reports final cumulative acceptance. totals covers the current attempt; runTotals is cumulative only with complete accounting. Unknown crash intervals are labeled, not invented. Output/task-wall throughput includes tools and checks. Buffered tool delivery is not GPU decode speed; stream metrics are null.
+
+Model-free tests exercise guarded edits, shared context, admission/tool waits, compaction/restart, immutable checker evidence, process-tree cancellation, provider errors and accounting. Run npm test --workspace @earendil-works/fleetpi from the fork root.
+
+See the host repository's integrations/fleetpi/README.md and INTERFACE.md for commands, API contracts, exact baselines, recording and provenance. Measured source is frozen separately from later reliability fixes.
